From: Tiago Damascena <tiagobdamascena@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 00:00:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] The controllers the launcher needs (RelicOS)

Two things the launcher (relicos-launch -> relicos-pads) needs from the
ES's %CONTROLLERSCONFIG% that a Linux build does not give:

- the device node of each pad (-pNpath). configureEmulators emits it
  only on WIN32; on Linux it is SDL_JoystickPathForIndex's
  /dev/input/eventN, the one name the ES and RetroArch's udev joypad
  driver share. -pNindex is SDL's order of appearance and RetroArch
  numbers pads by sysfs path on every launch, so a pad that arrives
  after the menu started (Bluetooth) has different numbers in the two.

- the handheld's own pad marked internal. computePlayersConfigs puts
  the internal controller last (unless system.input.p1_handheld), so a
  pad the user connects is player 1; the flag comes only from
  internal="1" in es_input.cfg, which KNULLI seeds and RelicOS does not
  (the ES writes the entry itself from SDL's mapping). "R36S Gamepad"
  (relicos-joypad) is internal by name, at construction and when an
  entry written without the flag is loaded.
---
diff -ruN a/es-core/src/InputConfig.cpp b/es-core/src/InputConfig.cpp
--- a/es-core/src/InputConfig.cpp	2026-09-13 11:07:40.668279291 -0300
+++ b/es-core/src/InputConfig.cpp	2026-09-13 11:07:40.682286011 -0300
@@ -122,6 +122,16 @@
 	mBatteryLevel = -1;
 	mIsWheel = false;
 	mIsInternal = false;
+#ifdef RELICOS
+	// The handheld's own pad (relicos-joypad's fused device) is the
+	// internal controller: last in computePlayersConfigs' order, so a pad
+	// the user connects becomes player 1 unless system.input.p1_handheld
+	// says otherwise -- KNULLI's rule, which its es_input.cfg seed states
+	// with internal="1". Decided by name here (and below, for an entry
+	// the ES wrote before this existed) since RelicOS seeds no entry.
+	if (deviceName == "R36S Gamepad")
+		mIsInternal = true;
+#endif
 	mDeviceParentSysPath = "";
 #ifdef HAVE_UDEV
 	mIsWheel = isWheel(devicePath);
@@ -283,6 +293,10 @@
 	// Determine whether the input device is an internal input device (e.g. built-in handheld controls)
 	pugi::xml_attribute attributeInternal = node.attribute("internal");
 	mIsInternal = attributeInternal.as_bool();
+#ifdef RELICOS
+	if (mDeviceName == "R36S Gamepad")
+		mIsInternal = true;
+#endif
 
 	for(pugi::xml_node input = node.child("input"); input; input = input.next_sibling("input"))
 	{
diff -ruN a/es-core/src/InputManager.cpp b/es-core/src/InputManager.cpp
--- a/es-core/src/InputManager.cpp	2026-09-13 11:07:40.666770830 -0300
+++ b/es-core/src/InputManager.cpp	2026-09-13 11:07:40.682164406 -0300
@@ -1199,7 +1199,10 @@
     if(playerInputConfig != NULL){
       command <<  "-p" << player+1 << "index "      << playerInputConfig->getDeviceIndex();
       command << " -p" << player+1 << "guid "       << playerInputConfig->getDeviceGUIDString();
-#if WIN32
+#if WIN32 || defined(RELICOS)
+	  // RelicOS: the launcher maps the pad to RetroArch's slot by its
+	  // device node (/dev/input/eventN), the one name SDL and RetroArch's
+	  // udev driver share; -pNindex is SDL's order, not RetroArch's.
 	  command << " -p" << player+1 << "path \""     << playerInputConfig->getDevicePath() << "\"";
 #endif
       command << " -p" << player+1 << "name \""     << playerInputConfig->getDeviceName() << "\"";
